{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["And the meaning of <b>the Levitical priests</b> is that they are the ones who say \"Cursed be the man.\" For the blessing — the sons of the mistresses; and for the curse — the sons of the maidservants. And if they be lacking two, the sons of Leah are many, and the great and the small were taken." "<b>And shall answer.</b> Like \"and you shall answer and say.\" And the Sages said that the meaning is to bless: \"Blessed be the man who does not make a graven or molten image,\" and so all of them. And according to the plain sense, the blessing is \"Blessed are you in the city,\" and the curse is the opposite of this. And the witness is in the book of Joshua."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:00.401009490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}